Subject: [PATCH] Tests: Wait for the URL after a crash during a blocked reload

After the renderer crashes in the middle of a blocked reload, the test
waits for the reloaded document's script to fetch from the server, and
then reads the current URL once. The script runs while the document is
still being parsed, before the navigation makes it the active document,
and the replacement renderer's active document until then is its
initial about:blank. So the read could see about:blank.

The same check for the reload without a crash passes either way, since
the document before it has the same URL. Wait for the URL instead, as
the test does elsewhere.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Tests/LibWebView/test-webdriver-session-history.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Tests/LibWebView/test-webdriver-session-history.py b/Tests/LibWebView/test-webdriver-session-history.py
index c5edcc7c5ab3733e565013203b1a2be1d0840753..5d41c1d580fa33fa22d06ff5d35bebb7c4c82dfa 100755
--- a/Tests/LibWebView/test-webdriver-session-history.py
+++ b/Tests/LibWebView/test-webdriver-session-history.py
@@ -5082,7 +5082,7 @@ return [Math.floor(rect.left + rect.width / 2), Math.floor(rect.top + rect.heigh
         )
         page_server.release_blocked_reload.set()
         wait_for_event(page_server.reload_blocked_document_ran, "reload document after crash recovery")
-        expect_url(webdriver_port, session_id, "after blocked reload crash recovery", url_reload_blocked, log)
+        wait_for_url(webdriver_port, session_id, "after blocked reload crash recovery", url_reload_blocked, log)
         wait_for_session_history(
             webdriver_port,
             session_id,
